14.114 emacsvox-eterm
=====================

This module makes eterm talk.  Eterm is the new terminal emulator for
Emacs.  Use of emacsvox with eterm really needs an info page.  At
present, the only documentation is the source level documentation.  This
module uses Control-t as an additional prefix key to allow the user To
move around the terminal and have different parts spoken.

14.114.1 Emacsvox-Eterm Commands
--------------------------------

14.114.1.1 emacsvox-eterm-copy-region-to-register
.................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-eterm-copy-region-to-register (register)

     Copy text from terminal to an Emacs REGISTER.
     This copies  region delimited by the emacsvox eterm marker
     set by command M-x emacsvox-eterm-set-marker and the
     emacsvox eterm pointer to a register.

     (fn REGISTER)

