   In addition, see commands in *Note emacsvox-google::, for
Google-Search specific commands, many of which are available via
prefix-key ‘G’.

14.117.7 Filtering Content Using XSLT And XPath
-----------------------------------------------

‘C-c’
     ‘emacsvox-we-junk-by-class-list’ Prompts for list of class-names
     with completion, and filters out matching elements.
‘C-f’
     ‘emacsvox-we-count-matches’ Prompts for XPath expression, and
     returns count of matching elements.
‘C-p’
     ‘emacsvox-we-xpath-junk-and-follow’ Follows link under point, and
     displays that page after filtering by a specified XPath expression.
‘C-t’
     ‘emacsvox-we-count-tables’ Display a count of tables in the page.
‘C-x’
     ‘emacsvox-we-count-nested-tables’ Counts nested tables.
‘C’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-by-class-list’ Prompts for a list of
     class-names, and displays matching elements.
‘D’
     ‘emacsvox-we-junk-by-class-list’ Filters out elements having
     specified class attributes.
‘I’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-by-id-list’ Extracts elements by specified
     list of ID values.
‘M’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-tables-by-match-list’ Extracts tables that
     match specified selection pattern.
‘P’
     ‘emacsvox-we-follow-and-extract-main’ Follows link under point, and
     extracts readable content, by default, this is all paragraphs and
     headings.
‘S’
     ‘emacsvox-we-style-filter’ Filters content by style attribute.
‘T’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-tables-by-position-list’ Extracts tables by
     their position on the page.
‘X’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-nested-table-list’ Extracts nested tables.
‘a’
     ‘emacsvox-we-xslt-apply’ Prompt for and apply specified XSLT
     transform to current page.
‘b’
     ‘emacsvox-we-follow-and-filter-by-id’ Follow link under point, and
     filter by specified id value.
‘c’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-by-class’ Extracts elements by class.
‘d’
     ‘emacsvox-we-junk-by-class’ Filters out elements having specified
     class value.
‘e’
     ‘emacsvox-we-url-expand-and-execute’ Follow link under point, but
     pass the result to a custom executor.  Availability of special
     executors for link under point is indicated by auditory icon *item*
     instead of *button* You can then experiment by pressing ‘RET’ or ‘e
     e’.  Special executors are available for Reddit Links, Wikipedia
     Links etc.
‘f’
     ‘emacsvox-we-xslt-filter’ Apply a specified XSLT filter (XPath) to
     current page.
‘i’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-by-id’ Extract elements by id value.
‘j’
     ‘emacsvox-we-xslt-junk’ Filter out elements matching specified
     pattern.
‘k’
     ‘emacsvox-we-toggle-xsl-keep-result’ Debugging tool -- retains the
     HTML source after XSLT.
‘m’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-table-by-match’ Extract matching table.
‘p’
     ‘emacsvox-we-xpath-follow-and-filter’ Follow link under point, and
     filter results by a specified XPath filter.
‘r’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-by-role’ Extract elements by specified role
     value.
‘s’
     ‘emacsvox-we-xslt-select’ Select default XSLT transform that is
     applied before rendering the page.
‘t’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-table-by-position’ Extracts tables by their
     position on the page.
‘u’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-matching-urls’ Display matching links on the
     page.
‘v’
     ‘emacsvox-we-class-follow-and-filter-link’ Follow link under point,
     and filter by specified class value.
‘w’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-by-property’ Extract element using a
     combination of DOM attributes.
‘x’
     ‘emacsvox-we-extract-nested-table’ Extract a nested table using a
     match-list.
‘y’
     ‘emacsvox-we-class-follow-and-filter’ Follow link under point and
     filter by class values.

14.117.8 EWW And EBooks On The Emacsvox Audio Desktop
-----------------------------------------------------

Modules emacsvox-epub and emacsvox-bookshare provide EBook front-ends to
EPub-2 and Daisy EBooks.  Both modules now use EWW to render these
EBooks.  Module emacsvox-eww provides a simple bookmarking facility --
called eww-marks (to avoid confusion with EWW's Web Bookmarks).  When
reading an EBook, you can use ‘m’ to create an EWW-mark at that
position.  These marks are automatically saved across Emacs sessions.
To open a previously created eww-mark, use command
‘emacsvox-eww-open-mark’ bound to ‘C-x r e’.  This command reads a
eww-mark name with completion.  Use this command with an interactive
prefix arg to delete a previously created eww-mark.

14.117.9 Extracting Readable Content
------------------------------------

By default, EWW includes a simple *readability* filter, ‘eww-readable’
bound to ‘s’.  Emacsvox extends this facility with ‘rdrview[ -- see
<https://github.com/eafer/rdrview>]’, a command-line tool that extracts
page contents using a *simplified view* filter that mirrors the
implementation in Firefox.

   You can use Emacsvox commands ‘emacsvox-eww-rdr- follow’ and
‘emacsvox-eww-rdr-reload’ both bound to ‘S’ with variable levels of
success on various Web sites.

